---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const resources = [
  {
    title: "About",
    description:
      "Discover the project's purpose, philosophy and architectural design.",
    href: "/about/",
  },
  {
    title: "Security",
    description:
      "Explore application permissions, access control and user authorization.",
    href: "/security/",
  },
  {
    title: "Development",
    description:
      "Learn about the architecture, technologies and engineering behind Y.Org.",
    href: "/development/",
  },
  {
    title: "Releases",
    description:
      "Explore version milestones, maintenance policies and long-term support.",
    href: "/releases/",
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout>
  <div class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Index</a>
  </div>

  <section class="welcome">
    <p class="eyebrow">THE Y.ORG PROJECT</p>

    <h1>Welcome to Y.Org</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      A Wayland compositor written in Rust, focused on
      security, application permissions and user control
      in Linux graphical environments.
    </p>

    <p>
      Y.Org (pronounced "Yorg") is an open-source project
      that provides a foundation for graphical sessions
      on Linux. Its architecture emphasizes transparency,
      security and a desktop experience in which users
      retain meaningful control over their environment.
    </p>

    <div class="welcome-links">
      <a
        class="primary-link"
        href="https://github.com/The-Y-Org-Project/Y.Org"
      >
        Explore the project <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>

      <a href="https://github.com/The-Y-Org-Project/Website">
        Website Source
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="content-layout">
    <article class="main-content">
      <section id="about" class="content-section">
        <h2>About the project</h2>

        <p>
          The graphical environment is a fundamental part
          of any desktop operating system. Y.Org provides
          an alternative approach to graphical session
          management, bringing together window composition,
          application interaction and user control.
        </p>

        <p>
          Written in Rust, Y.Org emphasizes reliability,
          security and a clear architectural foundation.
          It integrates these principles into the management
          of graphical surfaces and the interactions between
          applications and the desktop.
        </p>

        <p>
          Y.Org is an independent open-source project
          focused on building a transparent and
          user-oriented graphical environment for Linux.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/about/">Explore the about page →</a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="security" class="content-section">
        <h2>Security and permissions</h2>

        <p>
          Y.Org treats security as an important part of
          graphical session management. Applications do
          not automatically require unrestricted access
          to every capability available in the desktop
          environment.
        </p>

        <p>
          Its security model focuses on access control
          and explicit authorization for sensitive
          operations, including screen capture, input
          access and interactions that may expose private
          information or affect the user's session.
        </p>

        <p>
          By making access policies more transparent,
          Y.Org gives users a clearer understanding of
          application capabilities and the permissions
          associated with their graphical session.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/security/">Explore the security page →</a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="development" class="content-section">
        <h2>Development</h2>

        <p>
          Y.Org is developed in Rust, providing the
          foundation for its compositor architecture
          and graphical session management.
        </p>

        <p>
          The project uses Vunkan as its graphics-rendering
          technology, integrating rendering into its
          broader graphical architecture.
        </p>

        <p>
          Its development combines systems programming,
          graphical composition and security-oriented
          design. The source code and technical documentation
          provide insight into the project's implementation
          and architecture.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/development/">Explore the development page →</a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="releases" class="content-section">
        <h2>Releases and version lifecycle</h2>

        <p>
          Y.Org follows a progress-based version lifecycle.
          Each version is tracked from 0% at the beginning
          of its lifecycle to 100% at the end of its regular
          support period.
        </p>

        <p>
          Long-Term Support (LTS) versions extend this
          lifecycle to 150%. The additional 50% is dedicated
          exclusively to maintenance, including bug fixes
          and security updates. No new features are
          introduced during this extended support period.
        </p>

        <p>
          This approach separates regular development
          and maintenance from extended support, providing
          a clear distinction between feature development
          and long-term stability.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/releases/">Explore the releases page →</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>

    <aside class="sidebar" aria-label="Project information">
      <h2>Project resources</h2>

      {resources.map((resource) => (
        <div class="resource">
          <h3>
            <a href={resource.href}>{resource.title}</a>
          </h3>

          <p>{resource.description}</p>
        </div>
      ))}

      <div class="sidebar-status">
        <span
          class="status-indicator"
          aria-hidden="true"
        ></span>

        <span>Active Project</span>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <section class="project-notice">
    <strong>About this website</strong>

    <p>
      This is the official website of{" "}
      <a
        href="https://github.com/The-Y-Org-Project"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        The Y.Org Project
      </a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
